//
// LFM2-1.2B Q4NX prefill TTFT vs padded prefill length, into
// lfm2_1_2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// The other axis from run_npu2_sweep.lit: that one walks KV depth for decode
// tok/s, this one walks the length the prefill ELFs are BUILT for. They cannot
// share a table -- one is throughput against cache depth, the other is latency
// against problem size.
//
// The axis is the PADDED length, not the prompt length. These prefills pad the
// prompt to the built length and read the last real token's row, so at a fixed
// engine TTFT does not move with the prompt (llama32_1b_q4nx on a 2048 engine:
// 959 ms at 128 tokens, 983 ms at 2048). Every point here therefore rebuilds
// the prefill ELFs, and sweep_prefill.py fails the point rather than reporting
// a number if the engines came out at some other length.
//
// Unlike the decode sweep this needs real weights -- a prefill is a prefill --
// so it carries the same weight/token requirements as run_npu2_profile.lit.
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that); the
// per-length first-token argmax the driver already prints is recorded with
// each point because a bad build shows up there first.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23, hf_token, hfweights_liquidai_lfm2_1_2b
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name lfm2_1_2b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096 --seq-env LFM2_SEQ_LEN --bench-env LFM2_BENCH_L --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out lfm2_1_2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < lfm2_1_2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "lfm2_1_2b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's TTFT line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
